          %p
            The structure of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            also governs the existence of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            and the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebras"} ∞-Lie algebras
            such as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued forms
            with values in these constitute the field content of (11-dimensional)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %p
            Combining this, one finds that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            coupled to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            (super
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Yang-Mills+theories"} Einstein-Yang-Mills theories
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magic+pyramid"} magic pyramid
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%282%2CH%29"} SL(2,H)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+division+algebras"} supersymmetry and division algebras
            was gradually established by a variety of authors, including
          %ul
            %li#KugoTownsend82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taichiro+Kugo"}> Taichiro Kugo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and the division algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/181889"} spire:181889
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(83)90584-9"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(83)90584-9
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/140183/files/198301032.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Sudbery84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Sudbery"}> Anthony Sudbery
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division algebras, (pseudo)orthogonal groups and spinors
              %p
                939–955 (
                %a{:href => "\nhttps://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0305-4470/17/5/018"}> doi:10.1088/0305-4470/17/5/018
                )
            %li#Evans88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Evans"}> Jonathan Evans
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric Yang–Mills theories and division algebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "doi:10.1016/0550-3213(88)90305-7"} https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90305-7
            %li#ChungSudbery87
              %p
                K.-W. Chung,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Sudbery"} Anthony Sudbery
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Octonions and the Lorentz and conformal groups of ten-dimensional space-time
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91489-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91489-4
            %li#ManogueSudbery89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corinne+Manogue"}> Corinne Manogue
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Sudbery"} Anthony Sudbery
                = succeed "," do
                  %em General solutions of covariant superstring equations of motion
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.40.4073"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.40.4073
            %li#Schray96
              %p
                Jörg Schray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The general classical solution of the superparticle
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9407045"} arXiv:hep-th/9407045
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tevian+Dray"}> Tevian Dray
                , J. Janesky,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corinne+Manogue"} Corinne Manogue
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Octonionic hermitian matrices with non-real eigenvalues
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0006069"} arXiv:math/0006069
          %p
            Corresponding discussion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "twistor+space#TwistorSpace"} twistor space
          %ul
            %li#BengtssonCederwall88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"}> Ingemar Bengtsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Cederwall"} Martin Cederwall
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Particles, Twistors and the Division Algebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/247269"} spire
            %li#Cederwall93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Cederwall"}> Martin Cederwall
                ,
                %em Introduction to Division Algebras, Sphere Algebras and Twistors
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9310115"}> arXiv:hep-th/9310115
                )
          %p
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS
            version
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Arvanitakis"}> Alex Arvanitakis
              , Alec E. Barns-Graham,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twistor description of spinning particles in AdS
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.09557"} arXiv:1710.09557
          %p Streamlined proof and exposition:
          %ul
            %li#BaezHuerta09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division algebras and supersymmetry I
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                            %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*\ast
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 81
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0551"} arXiv:0909.0551
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PSPUM/81"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4887-6
            %li#BaezHuerta10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
                %strong 15
                (2011) 1373-1410 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"}> arXiv:1003.34360
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2011.v15.n5.a4"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2011.v15.n5.a4
          %p
            The case of 2-component quaternionic spinors in 6d (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%282%2CH%29"} SL(2,H)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jo%C3%A1s+Ven%C3%A2ncio"}> Joás Venâncio
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Batista"} Carlos Batista
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-Component Spinorial Formalism using Quaternions for Six-dimensional Spacetimes
              %strong 31
              71 (2021) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.04296"}> arXiv:2007.04296
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00006-021-01172-1"} doi:10.1007/s00006-021-01172-1
          %p
            Discussion with an emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freudenthal+magic+square"} Freudenthal magic square
          %ul
            %li#BorstenDuffHughesNagy13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leron+Borsten"}> Leron Borsten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mia+J.+Hughes"} Mia J. Hughes
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Silvia+Nagy"} Silvia Nagy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A magic square from Yang-Mills squared
                %strong 112
                (2014) 131601. &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4176"}> arXiv:1301.4176
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandros+Anastasiou"}> Alexandros Anastasiou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leron+Borsten"} Leron Borsten
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mia+J.+Hughes"} Mia J. Hughes
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Silvia+Nagy"} Silvia Nagy
                %em Super Yang-Mills, division algebras and triality
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.0546"}> arXiv:1309.0546
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#ABDHN
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandros+Anastasiou"}> Alexandros Anastasiou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leron+Borsten"} Leron Borsten
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mia+J.+Hughes"} Mia J. Hughes
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Silvia+Nagy"} Silvia Nagy
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A magic pyramid of supergravities
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6523"} arXiv:1312.6523
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mia+J.+Hughes"}> Mia J. Hughes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Octonions and Supergravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.25560/34938"} doi:10.25560/34938
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1756154"} inSpire:1756154
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://s3.cern.ch/inspire-prod-files-c/ccdb911a7f6c541e40164fffd84875ca"} pdf
          %p
            The relationship in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonion"} octonion
            algebra between the NRS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rafael I. Nepomechie,
                %em Nonabelian bosonization, triality, and superstring theory
                Physics Letters B Volume 178, Issues 2-3, 2 October 1986, Pages 207-210
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Itzhak+Bars"}> Itzhak Bars
                , D. Nemschansky and S. Yankielowicz, SLACPub-3758.
            %li
              %p
                H. Tachibana, K. Imeda,
                %em Octonions, superstrings and ten-dimensional spinors
                , Il nuovo cimento, Vol 104 B N.1
          %p
            The relation of the division algebras to ordinary (Lie algebraic) extensions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Jerzy Lukierski, Francesco Toppan,
                %em Generalized Space-time Supersymmetries, Division Algebras and Octonionic M-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0203149"}> arXiv:hep-th/0203149
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://cbpfindex.cbpf.br/publication_pdfs/NF00102.2010_08_03_10_47_48.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                A. Anastasiou, L. Borsten,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                %em An octonionic formulation of the M-theory algebra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1402.4649"}> arXiv:1402.4649
                )
          %p
            Normed division algebras are used to describe the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
            extensions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            in
          %ul
            %li#BH10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"} arXiv:1003.34360
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division Algebras, Supersymmetry and Higher Gauge Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.3385"} arXiv:1106.3385
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division Algebras and supersymmetry III
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3574"} arXiv:1109.3574
          %p
            This is made use of in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} homotopy theoretic description of M-theory
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+from+the+Superpoint"} M-Theory from the Superpoint
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.01774"} arXiv:1702.01774
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"}> John Huerta
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+homotopy+and+super+M-branes"} Real ADE-equivariant (co)homotopy and Super M-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.05987"}> arXiv:1805.05987
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Super-exceptional+M5-brane+model+--+Emergence+of+SU%282%29-flavor+sector"} Super-exceptional M5-brane model – Emergence of SU(2)-flavor sector
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.00012"}> arXiv:2006.00012
                )
        .revisedby
